  "story": {"premise": "At dawn, three facts must coexist before emergency traffic is released: the wind boundary is observed, the reconstructed bridge clock says the span is ready, and the hospital confirms the route. Repetition from any one subsystem is not progress, and two-of-three is no longer safe.", "submission": "Submit a PULSE program that emits once, with zero added latency, on the event that first completes all three distinct readiness topics. Preserve that decisive event's canonical payload.", "diagnostics": "The verifier exhausts every source-tagged stream of up to four signals over four ticks and distinguishes duplicate counting, two-of-three release, delayed all-topic completion, wrong payload, and refiring.", "hints": ["This is an all-three barrier, not the previous quorum.", "Set the current topic's bit before checking the other two.", "Seal the barrier after its first release."]}
